WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:13.040
62. Skateboarding. Sometime in the 1950s in California, surfers got bored. The water

2
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:20.180
was flat and still. They wanted something to surf, so they decided to surf the streets.

3
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:25.540
They took planks of wood, attached roller-skate wheels to them, and without knowing it, started

4
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:32.980
a new trend. Skateboarding was born. Of course, these surfers didn't know it yet. Skateboarding

5
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.900
was still called sidewalk surfing, and it was just something to do for fun when you

6
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:43.940
couldn't surf. The boards were basic and not very safe. People got hurt, but people

7
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:51.640
loved the new sport anyway. Throughout the 1950s and 1960s, skateboarding grew. Skateboarding

8
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:58.460
competitions were held and skate shops opened up. In 1972, proper skateboard wheels were

9
00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:06.260
developed, and boards became safer and lighter. In the 1950s and 1960s, skateboarding stuck

10
00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:12.540
close to the ground. However, in the 1970s, skaters began to use empty swimming pools

11
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:19.660
to get faster and higher. The age of vertical skate tricks was born. Over time, skaters

12
00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:25.740
created tricks like the ollie, jumping in the air without using your hands. Kick flips,

13
00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:30.780
keeping the board lengthwise while you are in the air, and slides or grinds, sliding

14
00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:37.740
down a rail on the board, among others. These tricks make skateboarding athletic, exciting,

15
00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:43.700
and fun to watch, but they also make it dangerous. The most common skateboarding injuries are

16
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:50.260
to the wrist, ankle, and face, but skateboarding can also cause serious head injuries. Nowadays,

17
00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:56.380
there are protective helmets and other gear to help prevent injuries. If you want to try this sport,

18
00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:02.020
which involves moving very quickly over hard surfaces, wearing something to protect your

19
00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.700
body is a good idea.
